vscode: double-click, Ctrl+C, double-click, Ctrl+V
open: order.spec.ts

@brief
Eight times: copy the word `CANCELLED` from the first line and paste it
over `PENDING` on the second, so both lines carry the same status.

A selection can be pasted over. `p` with a region highlighted replaces
the region with the register, and no `d` is needed first.

@keys
| `yiw` | yank the word under the cursor |
| `vi'` | select what is inside the quotes |
| `p` | replace the selection with the register |

@hints
`f'l` puts the cursor on the `C` of `CANCELLED`. `yiw` takes the word.
A search gets you to `PENDING`.
--
`vi'` selects the seven characters. `p` swaps them for the yanked word.
No delete, no insert mode, no `Esc`.

@solution
    f ' l y i w /PEND<Enter> v i ' p :wq<Enter>

Twenty keystrokes. `ciw` then typing the word is about the same length
for a nine-letter word and longer for a longer one, and it involves
typing a name you might mistype. Paste-over is the visual-mode idiom
that is genuinely hard to replace: select the wrong thing, `p` the
right thing on top.

One detail worth knowing. After a paste-over, the unnamed register
holds the text that was replaced — `PENDING` here, not `CANCELLED`. If
you want to paste the same word over several places, use `"0p` for the
second and later ones; chapter 20's yank register is exactly for this.

@start order.spec.ts
const target: OrderStatus = 'CANCELLED';
const order = { id: 'ord_1042', status: 'PENDING' };

@expected order.spec.ts
const target: OrderStatus = 'CANCELLED';
const order = { id: 'ord_1042', status: 'CANCELLED' };
